{"title":"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Background_Knowledge\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Background Knowledge</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Key_Lemma\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Key Lemma</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Proof_of_Key_Lemma\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof of Key Lemma</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#How_the_Key_Lemma_Solves_the_Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">How the Key Lemma Solves the Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(a) Prove that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/5/f35b4df2174c9e93d13d91ef893d3c1743e22e01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[5x]+[5y]\\ge [3x+y]+[3y+x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"248\" height=\"18\" />,</center>\n<p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef0b108cc310eb0dbbd5e0f930cdba3d178ebc84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/0/280a218bdb8d795b8bd3810c97c5b15a6cac3b2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[u]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the greatest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb30d1824269c52d9fd8ede8897e54aab111b3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> (e.g., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/9/6096210e09bfe83fe866eebcae8b65febbf1a331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\sqrt{2}]=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"22\" />).\n</p><p>(b) Using (a) or otherwise, prove that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adf3172b9cbf506283e6114ccb395d9c4901dcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(5m)!(5n)!}{m!n!(3m+n)!(3n+m)!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"194\" height=\"43\" /></center>\n<p>is integral for all positive integral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Background_Knowledge\">Background Knowledge</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Background Knowledge\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>Note: A complete proof for this problem may require these results, and preferably also their proofs.</i>\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496657d3096bd99c991b47be54f2b8cb872c13fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x] = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cd5e0ff89d918f22999f5b9c317b65b43b436f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\le x &lt; a + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" />. This is the alternate definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bceb7b14e55d33a8bca29b7863ad3cdae95afce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f8abc0d69ac6ab491f6125f9550af6b25e22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e14faf056c80898a02f856582a25660491e506.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a] \\le [b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />. This is easily proved by contradiction or consideration of the contrapositive.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/011a15570cb86dbe4151ff815e7c4e56f569dd0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x + a] = [x] + a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />. This is proved from considering that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db4374a23228afedad8cd263bd0341ea74bad517.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x] + a \\le x + a &lt; [x] + a + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>This is a known fact: the exponent of a prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0aeb9e9754601924ff2294e2db83a054e94a19bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\left[ \\frac{n}{p^k} \\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"64\" height=\"48\" />. (Legendre's Formula)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Key_Lemma\">Key Lemma</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Key Lemma\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>Lemma:</i> For any pair of non-negative real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, the following holds: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34bbc5e376a697221af34c5abd159ffcbc95896d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[5x] + [5y] \\ge [x] + [y] + [3x + y] + [3y + x].\\]\" width=\"336\" height=\"18\" />vcd\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_of_Key_Lemma\">Proof of Key Lemma</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Proof of Key Lemma\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We shall first prove the lemma statement for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/deee9aac0686c59a8b29a78db453f0bdd0b3b5f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le x, y &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af32349258a00bafeca8f9b6ddc67299b40381af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x] = [y] = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" />, and so we have to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/1/571b1ebec3f1a426c0580b3f40a21f7a4301929c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[5x] + [5y] \\ge [3x + y] + [3y + x].\\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfdde2e8d7b6b104d0b72ff8751265302837ad5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[5x] = a, [5y] = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />, for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd78eb8e64a18d6324d55c3f5fb8aaca46e5a0de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x &lt; a + 1 \\text{ and } 5y &lt; b + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"203\" height=\"16\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a81c8a66fc711b1c31653a2d10a4ddcd5ca16cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; \\frac{a+1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/1019cc5676a8d34b1c4e13577afd2ebe39424f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &lt; \\frac{b+1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>Define a new function, the ceiling function of x, to be the least integer greater than or equal to x. Also, define the <i>trun-ceil function</i>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a78d55bd79808ca63ec864744bbc27f5901bf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[[x]],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> to be the value of the ceiling function minus one. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6ccff027541df3a18dd8dd1cc16026dbc429f3b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[[a]] = a - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a70ea1a8f1a95b72639801b534c00305eb4e619f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[[a]] = [a]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> otherwise. It is not difficult to verify that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are real numbers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f8abc0d69ac6ab491f6125f9550af6b25e22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d847882d6df420ac6a1268e674802cad00be7d93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[[a]] \\le [a] \\le [[b]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />. (The only new thing we have to consider here is the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is integral, which is trivial.)\n</p><p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/491f72f77a3d96458f592930adc476a3612b265c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[3x + y] + [3y + x] \\le \\left [ \\left [\\frac{3a+b+4}{5} \\right ] \\right] + \\left[\\left[\\frac{3b+a+4}{5} \\right]\\right] = S.\\]\" width=\"471\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>We shall prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/8/3e8cdd67db7e31eb8365f69e66a35911f98e11a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\le a + b = T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />; to do so, we list cases. Without loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e1900f9ae83cebcbb5735f6c7bd6b6c505ba55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\le b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are less than one, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3b251089213622f203c8133f9b982e643e9c2d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\le b \\le 4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" /> Then, we find, for all 15 cases:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d61606a89acf72558c151a19e7da2706698720a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0, b = 0 \\rightarrow S = 0, T = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/d/eddac96afc540e3dae403ff2a517477e495dd6eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0, b = 1 \\rightarrow S = 1, T = 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5ae86e4cbb9db4053c3f56cb93051becfa110b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0, b = 2 \\rightarrow S = 2, T = 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/65761b3138186057d1c740e28dffd4f018d14e38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0, b = 3 \\rightarrow S = 3, T = 3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d8c71ae76338e02ac76b13e20a435f886802df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0, b = 4 \\rightarrow S = 4, T = 4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f8430e2f88424a73510c27efd2c3944766f150ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1, b = 1 \\rightarrow S = 2, T = 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cf9a6b1d045ad506addab61b7038800202c3840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1, b = 2 \\rightarrow S = 3, T = 3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb6007e8b8b98dd75fd4fe6ef342815d37ec2edb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1, b = 3 \\rightarrow S = 3, T = 4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c7d6c6b7c9dd743ecac7488db773207c318709b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1, b = 4 \\rightarrow S = 5, T = 5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a44bd4c08d97022ff5a1c099c71db3c9d3a07c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2, b = 2 \\rightarrow S = 4, T = 4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52bf603bb4ebf2c765f6b9fe8d198e4b7515bb6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2, b = 3 \\rightarrow S = 4, T = 5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/6/2162679cb79ab1e580498649f508d53fdcd3abe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2, b = 4 \\rightarrow S = 5, T = 6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/757e2ab24e05ee0a9a3e9876086a0c927b1ea616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3, b = 3 \\rightarrow S = 6, T = 6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/8/c38bb170f66d753e2f6fad357f748f90a8cd9aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3, b = 4 \\rightarrow S = 6, T = 7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/48778981cd506d70fac9e9bc5a80e08d6d3244e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 4, b = 4 \\rightarrow S = 6, T = 8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Thus, we have proved for all x and y in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/0004bfe2d7fa21b99eaf702d39b6de356c7915a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6ca196db7d5557b2f8d7d48e3f580c7b42ee1d50.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[5x] + [5y] = T \\ge S \\ge [3x + y] + [3y + x].\\]\" width=\"325\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Now, we prove the lemma statement without restrictions on x and y. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7ba3659386340458fb4b465396ee01ffbb6d452c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = [x] + \\{x\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"19\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa4994e7a93f59b0f51811412d58963d91178918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = [y] + \\{y\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df2919191b1220773d9b0142dec5c3528fd4c42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />, the fractional part of x, is defined to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1dbe062f098f5f644a2181493823636dbeddb7eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - [x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/35698e01e51d800ae9309a1e55ec0c3ab533d1cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x\\} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> as a result. Substituting gives the equivalent inequality\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6b7f3ac15f39a3d13625848ab8a822028afe238.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[5[x] + 5\\{x\\}] + [5[y] + 5\\{y\\}] \\ge [x] + [y] + [3[x] + 3\\{x\\} + [y] + \\{y\\}] + [3[y] + 3\\{y\\} + [x] + \\{x\\}].\\]\" width=\"637\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>But, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/6/d96ff1b577c91e6300341d68b843a9255ba0cd22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x] + a = [x + a]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, this is obtained from simplifications following the adding of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/8/af87db6bca1e37b97788f9659acf18bf01326ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5[x] + 5[y]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" /> to both sides of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f823cb194f79c5c7a282308f548a8b8df2066530.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[5\\{x\\}] + [5\\{y\\}] \\ge [3\\{x\\} + \\{y\\}] + [3\\{y\\} + \\{x\\}],\\]\" width=\"360\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>which we have already proved (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb2291eebb4d18e3358f46fb10d6a493983ba20f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le \\{x\\}, \\{y\\} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />). Thus, the lemma is proved.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"How_the_Key_Lemma_Solves_the_Problem\">How the Key Lemma Solves the Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: How the Key Lemma Solves the Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Part (a) is a direct corollary of the lemma.\n</p><p>For part (b), consider an arbitrary prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. We have to prove the exponent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa6effc911895fe1df8d2041e7d5bab905e0e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I = \\frac{(5m)!(5n)!}{m!n!(3m+n)!(3n+m)!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"227\" height=\"43\" /></center>\n<p>is non-negative, or equivalently that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/55676a2d22ad00847a01b71e2a726805a3bf2446.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\left( \\left[ \\frac{5m}{p^k} \\right] + \\left[ \\frac{5n}{p^k} \\right] \\right) \\ge \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\left( \\left[ \\frac{m}{p^k} \\right] + \\left[ \\frac{n}{p^k} \\right] + \\left[ \\frac{3m+n}{p^k} \\right] + \\left[ \\frac{3n+m}{p^k} \\right] \\right).\\]\" width=\"561\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>But, the left-hand side minus the right-hand side of this inequality is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c20a47cef89744b5f1f88a36db9329a2119138cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\left( \\left[ \\frac{5m}{p^k} \\right] + \\left[ \\frac{5n}{p^k} \\right] - \\left[ \\frac{m}{p^k} \\right] - \\left[ \\frac{n}{p^k} \\right] - \\left[ \\frac{3m+n}{p^k} \\right] - \\left[ \\frac{3n+m}{p^k} \\right] \\right),\\]\" width=\"505\" height=\"48\" /> which is the sum of non-negative terms by the Lemma. Thus, the inequality is proved, and so, by considering all primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we deduce that the exponents of all primes in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are non-negative. This proves the integrality of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO\" title=\"1975 USAMO\">1975 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1975\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172032\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 468/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16296/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.392      1 -total\n 60.14%    8.054      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 37.25%    4.989      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7534:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172032 and revision id 220219. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}